      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 778095789,
      "version": 650,
      "versionNonce": 2083127821,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784703810795,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How to optimise storage of our system?\n- We're indexing huge amt of data but our users will be interested in very small portion of it\n- put caps and limits on each of our inverted indexes, we won't need all 10M posts with \"Mark\" contained somewhere in their content. Keep indexes size to 1k-10k items\n- Most keywords won't be searched often at all, based on search analytics run batch job to move rarely searched keywords to S3 or R2\n- First query Redis, if not matched then query index stored in S3 with small latency",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How to optimise storage of our system?\n- We're indexing huge amt of data but our users will be interested in very small portion of it\n- put caps and limits on each of our inverted indexes, we won't need all 10M posts with \"Mark\" contained somewhere in their content. Keep indexes size to 1k-10k items\n- Most keywords won't be searched often at all, based on search analytics run batch job to move rarely searched keywords to S3 or R2\n- First query Redis, if not matched then query index stored in S3 with small latency",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
